# =====================================================================
#  Whitelist policy: everything is ignored unless explicitly allowed.
#
#  Rationale: this repository sits next to copyrighted study materials
#  (commercial exam-prep books in PDF). A blacklist would only protect
#  against the files we thought of in advance; a whitelist protects
#  against every file nobody thought of. A new PDF dropped into this
#  folder cannot reach the index.
#
#  Adding a new tracked file REQUIRES adding an explicit "!" rule here.
# =====================================================================

*

# --- root pages -------------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!CLAUDE.md
!README.md
!LICENSE
!index.html
!reference.html
!exam-map.html
!sources.html
!su[0-9][0-9].html
!trainer.html
!build_artifact.py

# --- assets: open the directory, then allow files one by one ----------
!assets/
assets/*
!assets/style.css
!assets/app.js
!assets/modules.js
!assets/trainer.js
!assets/figures-2025.js
!assets/quiz-su[0-9][0-9].js

# =====================================================================
#  Hard bans. Listed last so they win over every "!" rule above.
# =====================================================================

# Study materials and any other PDF must never be committed.
*.pdf

# Local-only overlays (e.g. cross-references to commercial textbooks).
# These exist on the author's disk only and are not part of the project.
*.local.js

# Generated single-file build. An artifact, not a source.
ea-part2.html
